{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788594153198877001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"yummy-yogic-clam","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"218b53428e18e3ff41cb838f325c5c8ac770422e7c44f6d68b0a62209e28160e","event_uuid":"cf16f1e2-098e-4a91-a031-b506fe2655c9","position":{"commit_sha":"120df7334d422a8279c2ca12ef6380ad028e154c","position":"1788589242474082001-cf16f1e2-098e-4a91-a031-b506fe2655c9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788589242474082001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## What is confirmed\n\nAn agent's ticket writes were **lost** and survived only because it also described them in its\nprose report. Specifically, on `torrential-unwhite-snail` (`9c2e-b44c-119e-4105`) the agent:\n\n- retitled the ticket and raised it to priority 2, and\n- posted a root-cause comment containing a fully reproduced diagnosis (the four-xdist-workers /\n  four-gate-slots exhaustion, with a serial-vs-parallel experiment).\n\nNeither reached the shared store. Verified directly afterwards: the ticket was still **priority 3\nwith 1 comment**, its original state. The finding was recoverable only because I could re-derive it\nfrom the agent's report text and re-verify its three load-bearing facts against `origin/main`\nmyself.\n\nThat is a data-loss path through the shared record. The next agent to hit it may not restate its\nfindings in prose, and then the work is simply gone.\n\n## The reported mechanism — RELAYED, and NOT currently reproducible\n\nThe agent reported that its worktree's ticket-store clone had diverged from `origin/tickets` with\n**no shared history**, `rebar fsck` saying *\"The local store was built independently of the remote\n... its writes will never push\"*, and **2,492 unpushed commits across 142 distinct tickets**.\n\nI could not reproduce this. Checking three agent worktrees minutes later:\n\n    fix-acli-ceiling-partition        in sync      <- the very worktree that reported divergence\n    bug-9c93-ad8d-user-data-mounts    in sync\n    fix-b2ff-mcp-readonly-empty       ahead/behind (shared history, normal)\n\nand the shared store on the main checkout was `local HEAD == origin/tickets`, with `rebar fsck`\nreporting **no divergence line at all**. So the condition was transient and had healed by the time\nI looked. The 2,492/142 figures are the agent's measurement, not mine, and I am recording them as\nrelayed rather than established.\n\n## The one thing that worked, worth preserving\n\nThe failure was **loud at the end**: the agent's final two writes were REFUSED, with `fsck` naming\nthe condition and the remedy. That is why the agent noticed at all. Whatever the fix, keep that —\na silent local-only accumulation would be far worse than a refusal.\n\nBut note the asymmetry that produced the loss: writes made BEFORE the refusal appeared to succeed\nlocally and were stranded silently. Only the last two were refused. So \"loud on refusal\" is not the\nsame as \"loud on divergence\".\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Reproduce the divergence deliberately in a scratch worktree, or establish that it cannot\n      recur and say why. This ticket rests on a relayed observation; the first job is to make it\n      first-hand or refute it. A refutation is a valid outcome — close it as `not_a_bug` with the\n      evidence.\n- [ ] Determine whether a worktree created by `make worktree` gets its own tracker clone, and\n      whether that clone can be built independently of the remote (the `fsck` text and the\n      `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` note both point at a re-clone that did not carry `.env-id` /\n      `.opcert-key` / `.ensure-applied`).\n- [ ] A store that CANNOT push is detected at the first write, not the last. Proven by driving a\n      write against a deliberately-diverged clone and observing the refusal on write #1.\n- [ ] If stranded commits are recoverable, the recovery path is documented and does not require an\n      operator to reconstruct findings from an agent's prose. `rebar fsck-recover` exists but is\n      mutating; establish whether it preserves stranded events or discards them, because those are\n      very different remedies when 142 tickets' worth of another session's work is involved.\n- [ ] The interaction with concurrent sessions is stated: this host runs eleven worktrees against\n      one shared `tickets` branch, and any recovery that rewrites shared history is unsafe while\n      others are writing.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2d52-5abe-abb8-44ab","ticket_type":"bug","title":"An agent's ticket writes were stranded and lost: a retitle and a fully-reproduced root-cause comment never reached the shared store, recoverable only from the agent's prose report","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cf16f1e2-098e-4a91-a031-b506fe2655c9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788594153198877001,"uuid":"2288e8a9-9b28-4e34-b553-51c74c2069d3"}